# M4.24 static guard false-positive diagnosis

Date: 2026-08-28

## Failure

The first M4.24 CI guard searched broadly for `systemctl` near `enable` or for
`WantedBy=`. It matched the controller's read-only `is-enabled` observation and
the code that explicitly rejects a `WantedBy=` unit. Those are safety checks,
not activation behavior.

The combined local validation also placed commands after the negated grep, so
the later successful command hid that guard's nonzero final status. GitHub CI
would not have hidden it because the grep is a dedicated step.

## Impact

No forbidden start persistence, enable or restart behavior exists. The
dedicated unit test already rejects literal `SYSTEMCTL, "enable"` and
`SYSTEMCTL, "restart"` command construction. No repository, GitHub or server
state changed.

## Correction and rollback

The CI regex now targets only actual Python command argument sequences for
`enable` or `restart`, while retaining broad-deletion, provider-credential,
external-API and cron rejection. The local rerun uses an explicit conditional
whose failure cannot be masked by later commands. Rollback is the normal Git
revert for this still-unactivated branch.
